          "tz": -480
        },
        "subject": "LU-21061 lod: allocate directory stripes from pool MDTs",
        "message": "LU-21061 lod: allocate directory stripes from pool MDTs\n\nThe MDTs of a pool do not limit where the stripes of a directory go.\nlod_mdt_alloc_qos(), lod_mdt_alloc_rr() and lod_mdt_alloc_specific()\nchoose among all MDTs, ignoring the pool of the directory layout and\nof the parent default LMV.\n\nRecord in lod_ah_init() the pool of a new directory: the pool it was\ngiven, or else the pool of the parent default LMV.  Allocate the\nstripes other than the local master from the MDTs of that pool, with\na round-robin list of their own.  Count only those MDTs to limit the\nstripe count and to decide whether a directory is overstriped.  A pool\nthat lists no MDTs does not limit the stripes.\n\nTest-Parameters: mdscount=2 mdtcount=4 testlist=ost-pools\nSigned-off-by: Di Wang <diwa@nvidia.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5 ltvm\nChange-Id: I14948c6e4b833422010f46df7e960369baacb56e\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
